## Synthetic. Same discontinuity as hls-media-pdt-discontinuity.m3u8, but the
## packager does the right thing and emits a fresh #EXT-X-PROGRAM-DATE-TIME
## immediately after it, re-anchoring the timeline.
##
## Note the second PDT is NOT what accumulating across the discontinuity
## would have predicted (13:59:36Z) — the splice drops 4 seconds. That gap is
## exactly why durations can't be composed across a discontinuity, and a test
## reading 13:59:40Z off the second asset proves the re-anchor is honoured
## rather than the arithmetic.
#EXTM3U
#EXT-X-TARGETDURATION:7
#EXT-X-VERSION:3
#EXT-X-MEDIA-SEQUENCE:661500
#EXT-X-PROGRAM-DATE-TIME:2026-09-10T13:59:24.000Z
#EXTINF:6.000,
https://live-content.xumo.com/3845/content/XM08RIB78GYPVR/28846714/6_300.ts
#EXTINF:6.000,
https://live-content.xumo.com/3845/content/XM08RIB78GYPVR/28846714/6_301.ts
#EXT-X-DISCONTINUITY
#EXT-X-PROGRAM-DATE-TIME:2026-09-10T13:59:40.000Z
#EXTINF:6.000,
https://live-content-cf.xumo.com/149/content/XM05M7E0PC09SI/28980908/6_020.ts
#EXTINF:6.000,
